# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Comprobar el estado {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Inmediatamente después de llamar a `run()`, el estado suele ser `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Estado | Significado |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | El trabajo espera un espacio de cómputo. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | El flujo de trabajo está iniciando un entorno con el perfil de cómputo del trabajo. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | Se está ejecutando el punto de entrada del flujo de trabajo. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | El punto de entrada informó de una etapa con [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), como `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Cancelaste el trabajo y el flujo de trabajo lo está deteniendo. |\n"
"| `DONE` | El punto de entrada terminó correctamente. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | El punto de entrada generó un error o terminó con un código distinto de cero. Consulta [Encontrar la causa de un error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Cancelaste el trabajo, o alcanzó el [límite de 24 horas](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR` y `CANCELED` son estados finales, y `job.in_terminal_state()` devuelve `True` para ellos. Un bucle de estado que espera otro valor, como `SUCCEEDED`, nunca termina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Esperar a que termine el trabajo {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Para esperar hasta que el trabajo termine, llama a `wait_for_final_state()`. Devuelve el estado final y, con `verbose=True`, imprime cada cambio de estado. Si estableces `timeout` en segundos, `wait_for_final_state()` genera un `TimeoutError` cuando se agota el tiempo antes de que termine el trabajo. El trabajo sigue ejecutándose:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` comprueba el estado después de 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 y 32 segundos, y luego cada 60 segundos, de modo que detecta el final de un trabajo corto en cuestión de segundos y realiza pocas solicitudes en un trabajo largo. Para comprobar a un intervalo fijo en su lugar, pasa `poll_interval` en segundos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Leer los registros {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Todo lo que el flujo de trabajo escribe en la salida estándar o en el error estándar va a los registros del trabajo. Puedes leerlos con `job.logs()` mientras el trabajo se ejecuta, antes de que tenga un resultado:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "El flujo de trabajo carga las líneas de registro nuevas aproximadamente cada 15 segundos, y una última vez cuando el trabajo termina o se cancela. Inmediatamente después de que un trabajo comienza, `job.logs()` devuelve `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "El flujo de trabajo conserva los 50 MB más recientes de registros de cada trabajo y añade una línea al principio que indica que los registros se truncaron.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Para decidir qué registra tu flujo de trabajo, consulta [Escribir registros](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Para mostrar solo las líneas que coinciden con una expresión regular, pasa `include` a `job.filtered_logs()`. Para ocultar líneas, pasa `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Obtener el resultado {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` espera hasta que el trabajo termina y luego devuelve el valor que el flujo de trabajo pasó a [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "De forma predeterminada, `job.result()` comprueba el estado cada 30 segundos y espera sin límite de tiempo. Pasa `maxwait` para limitar el número de comprobaciones. Por ejemplo, `job.result(maxwait=40)` espera unos 20 minutos. Para comprobar una sola vez sin esperar, pasa `wait=False`. Si `job.result()` deja de esperar antes de que el trabajo termine, devuelve `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Comprobar cuánto duró cada etapa {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` enumera cada cambio de estado y de etapa de un trabajo con su hora, para que puedas ver cuánto esperó el trabajo por el cómputo y cuánto duró cada etapa:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Los eventos usan los nombres de estado almacenados. `PENDING` es `INITIALIZING`, y `SUCCEEDED` es `DONE`. Para consultar el uso de QPU de una ejecución, consulta [Encontrar los trabajos de QPU de una ejecución](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Encontrar la causa de un error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando el flujo de trabajo genera una excepción, el trabajo termina con el estado `ERROR`. Por ejemplo, ejecuta el flujo de trabajo con un ángulo que rechaza:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Los registros muestran el traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Si el flujo de trabajo [informa de errores con `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), léelos con `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` y lee sus mensajes con `job.error_message()`. Para un trabajo sin errores informados, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` devuelve una lista vacía y `job.error_message()` devuelve `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Gestionar trabajos {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Cancelar un trabajo {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Cancela un trabajo con `job.cancel()`. El estado cambia a `CANCELING` mientras el flujo de trabajo detiene el trabajo y, después, a `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` devuelve un mensaje sobre el trabajo y sobre sus [trabajos de QPU vinculados](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), que también intenta cancelar. Para un trabajo en ejecución, el flujo de trabajo envía `SIGTERM` a tu punto de entrada. Para guardar resultados parciales, consulta [Limpiar cuando se cancela un trabajo](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Si el trabajo ya terminó, `job.cancel()` devuelve `Job already in terminal state.` y no cambia nada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Encontrar un trabajo desde una sesión nueva {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"El objeto `Job` y el flujo de trabajo existen solo en tu sesión actual de Python. Después de reiniciar el kernel de un notebook, pasa el ID de trabajo guardado a `client.job()`, o enumera tus trabajos recientes con `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` devuelve tus 10 trabajos más recientes, los más nuevos primero. Fíltralos con `function`, `status` (de la [tabla de estados](#check-the-status)) o `created_after` (una marca de tiempo ISO 8601), y pagínalos con `limit` y `offset`. Para enumerar los flujos de trabajo que cargaste, llama a `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "La tabla [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) de IBM Quantum Platform también enumera tus trabajos, con su estado, perfil de cómputo y tiempos de ejecución.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Límite de tiempo {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Un flujo de trabajo gestionado cancela un trabajo que se ejecuta durante más de 24 horas, y el trabajo termina con el estado `CANCELED`. Durante las ejecuciones largas, [guarda puntos de control en el almacenamiento de archivos](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) para no perder trabajo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Solucionar problemas de trabajos {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` falla con `Code: 429` y `Active job limit reached.` | Alcanzaste el [límite de trabajos activos](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Espera a que terminen algunos trabajos o [cancela](#cancel-a-job) los que ya no necesites. |\n"
"| El trabajo permanece en `QUEUED`, y `run()` advirtió que `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | El trabajo no se inicia hasta que se levante el bloqueo de tu cuenta, plan o suscripción. Contacta con tu administrador. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` devuelve `No logs yet.` | El trabajo está en cola o acaba de empezar. Espera unos 15 segundos. |\n"
"| `job.result()` devuelve `{}` | El trabajo no ha terminado, se canceló o no guardó ningún resultado. Consulta [Guardar resultados](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` devuelve `{}` | El flujo de trabajo generó una excepción sin informar de un error. Lee el traceback con `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| El trabajo está en `CANCELED`, pero no lo cancelaste | El trabajo alcanzó el [límite de 24 horas](#time-limit). |\n"

